   "**A travel warning is an economic verdict issued on a case count** — the direct effect is cancelled itineraries and conferences; the compound consequence is that advisories are imposed on numbers and lifted on nothing in particular, so tourism and air links recover more slowly than the outbreak — a country that contained nine cases can carry the cost of a thousand for a year, and that cost is itself a cause of the next outbreak's underfunding",
