  "hinge": "The cause is not the virus and it is not the border. It is the choice — by Kenya's health ministry, whether the cluster is closed by a complete, paid, published tracing operation in the next fortnight; by Nigeria and Uganda, whether the genetic link is followed as one regional investigation rather than three national ones with separate press lines; by the hospitals that treated the index patient before diagnosis, whether triage and isolation are rebuilt now rather than after the next undiagnosed arrival; by the trial sponsors, whether a Bundibugyo candidate moves at the speed of an outbreak; and by the governments issuing travel advisories, whether the advisory is proportionate to the cases counted. §2 puts the duty where the money is: help for the sick and suffering is not charity, it is the cause that changes the effect. Whether Kenya's first outbreak ends at nine cases or becomes its first epidemic is not fixed by the species; it is a decision held by named ministers, named hospital directors and named donors, and one that a different choice could still make."
